      "content": "#include <cstdio>\n#include <memory>\n#include <vector>\n\nclass FastScanner {\n    static constexpr int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\n    char* cur;\n    char* end;\n\n    bool refill() {\n        size_t r = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n        cur = buf;\n        end = buf + r;\n        return r > 0;\n    }\n\npublic:\n    FastScanner() : cur(buf), end(buf) {}\n\n    inline int nextInt() {\n        while (true) {\n            if (cur == end && !refill()) return 0;\n            char c = *cur++;\n            if (c <= ' ') continue;\n\n            int sign = 1;\n            if (c == '-') {\n                sign = -1;\n                if (cur == end && !refill()) return 0;\n                c = *cur++;\n            }\n\n            int x = c - '0';\n            while (true) {\n                if (cur == end && !refill()) break;\n                char d = *cur++;\n                if (d < '0' || d > '9') break;\n                x = x * 10 + (d - '0');\n            }\n            return sign * x;\n        }\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\n\n    const size_t ringSize = (size_t)s + 1;\n    std::unique_ptr<int[]> storage(new int[ringSize * (size_t)n]);\n    int* __restrict ring = storage.get();\n\n    std::vector<long long> col(n, 0);\n    long long* __restrict c = col.data();\n    std::vector<int> tmpVec(n);\n    int* __restrict tmp = tmpVec.data();\n\n    // Read first s rows.\n    // First row: initialize column sums directly (B's idea).\n    {\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 3 < n; j += 4) {\n            int v0 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v1 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v2 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v3 = fs.nextInt();\n            tmp[j] = v0; tmp[j+1]=v1; tmp[j+2]=v2; tmp[j+3]=v3;\n        }\n        for (; j < n; ++j) tmp[j] = fs.nextInt();\n        int* row0 = ring;\n        #pragma omp simd\n        for (int k=0;k<n;++k) { row0[k]=tmp[k]; c[k]=tmp[k]; }\n    }\n    // Remaining s-1 rows.\n    for (int r = 1; r < s; ++r) {\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 3 < n; j += 4) {\n            int v0 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v1 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v2 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v3 = fs.nextInt();\n            tmp[j] = v0; tmp[j+1]=v1; tmp[j+2]=v2; tmp[j+3]=v3;\n        }\n        for (; j < n; ++j) tmp[j] = fs.nextInt();\n        int* row = ring + (size_t)r * n;\n        #pragma omp simd\n        for (int k=0;k<n;++k) { row[k]=tmp[k]; c[k]+=tmp[k]; }\n    }\n\n    // Evaluate horizontal windows for the first top row.\n    long long best = 0;\n    {\n        long long hsum = 0;\n        for (int j=0;j<s;++j) hsum += c[j];\n        if (hsum > best) best = hsum;\n        for (int j=s;j<n;++j) {\n            hsum += c[j] - c[j-s];\n            if (hsum > best) best = hsum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    const int mod = s + 1;\n    // Slide vertically.\n    for (int i = s; i < n; ++i) {\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 3 < n; j += 4) {\n            int v0 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v1 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v2 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v3 = fs.nextInt();\n            tmp[j] = v0; tmp[j+1]=v1; tmp[j+2]=v2; tmp[j+3]=v3;\n        }\n        for (; j < n; ++j) tmp[j] = fs.nextInt();\n\n        const int slot = i % mod;\n        const int oldSlot = (i - s) % mod;\n        int* pi = ring + (size_t)slot * n;\n        const int* po = ring + (size_t)oldSlot * n;\n\n        #pragma omp simd\n        for (int k=0;k<n;++k) {\n            int v = tmp[k];\n            pi[k] = v;\n            c[k] += (long long)v - po[k];\n        }\n\n        // Evaluate horizontal windows.\n        long long hsum = 0;\n        for (int j=0;j<s;++j) hsum += c[j];\n        if (hsum > best) best = hsum;\n        for (int j=s;j<n;++j) {\n            hsum += c[j] - c[j-s];\n            if (hsum > best) best = hsum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", (long long)best);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Integrating B's direct column-sum initialization from the first row, C's temporary row buffer to decouple I/O from computation, and A's ring-buffer rolling sums with sequential single-pass horizontal window evaluation (avoiding per-row OpenMP thread overhead) yields lower runtime than any single archived transformation.",
  "notes": "The candidate combines all three source ideas: it uses a flat circular ring buffer for the last S+1 rows (A), initializes column sums by copying the first row directly and then adding the remaining S-1 rows (B), buffers each input row into a temporary vector before updating the ring and column sums (C), and evaluates horizontal windows with an incremental single-pass scan per top row instead of spawning OpenMP threads inside the vertical loop. SIMD pragmas are placed on independent loops to encourage vectorization while keeping the critical path sequential.",
